issue_context.body:
The `DisposeAsync` is being called twice by DI (at least when using the generic host) if the call is asynchronous and only once if it does not have `await`s and executes synchronously. Is it the desired behavior? Any advice on where to look for an explanation of this behavior is appreciated.

### To Reproduce
```csharp
public sealed class NewService : IAsyncDisposable
{
    public NewService(ILogger<NewService>? logger)
    {
        this.logger = logger;
        logger?.LogInformation("The instance was created.");
    }

    public async ValueTask DisposeAsync()
    {
        using var scope = logger?.BeginScope("Disposing the new service asynchronosusly.");

        await Task.Delay(1); // if commented out, the DisposeAsync is being called only once
        
        logger?.LogInformation("The service is disposed.");
    }        

    private readonly ILogger? logger;
}
```

```csharp
static async Task Main(string[] args)
{
    var configuration = new ConfigurationBuilder()
        .AddJsonFile("appsettings.json")
        .Build();

    using var host = new HostBuilder()
        .ConfigureLogging(builder => builder.AddSerilog(
            new LoggerConfiguration()
                .ReadFrom.Configuration(configuration)
                .CreateLogger()))
        .ConfigureServices(services => services
            .AddSingleton<NewService>())
            .Build();

    await host.StartAsync();

    _ = host.Services.GetService<NewService>();
}
```
1) Register the class above as a singleton for generic host;
2) Resolve the reference to the service;
3) Exit the application.

### Expected behavior
The `DisposeAsync` is called once.

### Additional context
If the `await Task.Delay(1);` is commented out and the method becomes synchronous, it's being executed only once.

